  "releaseNotes": "8.1.0\n\n\t\t\tNew primitive: +/- to negate a number (e.g. 5 +/- ==> -5)\n\t\t\tNew error: OperationNotSupportedError (MW.7)\n\n\t\t\tforeach now supports a transform mode:\n\t\t\t(1 2 3 4) foreach 'item' transform { item 2 * }       ==> (2 4 6 8)\n\t\t\t(1 2 3 4) foreach 'item' transform { item 2 * ->str } ==> (\"2\" \"4\" \"6\" \"8\")\n\n\t\t\tMOGBaseItems and MOGRecord now expose typed helper methods (AddString, AddNumber, AddName... / SetString, SetNumber, SetName...) that simplify object creation without requiring an explicit Engine reference.\n\n\t\t\tChanged: get on MOGRecord now returns MOGNull instead of throwing when key is not found.\n\t\t\tChanged: keys named after reserved words are now allowed.\n\n\t\t\tFixed: bug with MOGRecord AutoEval capability.",
